 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nColumn qualification broken for struct field access\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen qualifying columns that contain struct field access (dot notation), the column qualification logic is not working properly. This affects queries with struct fields where the column should be qualified with the appropriate table alias.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimizer\n\n# Example with struct field access\nquery = \"select a.b:c from d\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(query, read='snowflake')\nqualified = optimizer.qualify.qualify(parsed)\nprint(qualified.sql())\n```\n\nThe column qualification should properly handle struct field access patterns but currently fails to qualify the columns correctly.\n\nThis also affects BigQuery queries with struct field access:\n\n```python\nquery = \"SELECT a, a.b, a.b.c FROM x, UNNEST(x.a) AS a\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(query, read='bigquery')\nqualified = optimizer.qualify.qualify(parsed, schema={'x': {'a': 'ARRAY<STRUCT<b STRUCT<c int>>>'}})\nprint(qualified.sql())\n```\n\nThe issue appears to be related to how the column qualification logic handles dot notation in column references when determining if a column needs to be qualified with a table name.\n</issue>\n",
